WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.595
A bright yellow solution turns orange when

00:00:03.595 --> 00:00:06.390
cyanide is introduced. But does the colour

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:09.186
change actually identify one ion, or only

00:00:09.186 --> 00:00:10.783
something about the mixture?

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.909
This is the published experiment, not a

00:00:18.909 --> 00:00:22.018
substitute stock photograph. The four panels record

00:00:22.018 --> 00:00:25.127
absorption, visible colour, fluorescence emission, and the

00:00:25.127 --> 00:00:26.904
vials under ultraviolet light.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.752
The test was in ninety percent acetonitrile

00:00:33.752 --> 00:00:36.704
and ten percent water. Curcumin began yellow,

00:00:36.704 --> 00:00:39.655
while added cyanide produced a striking orange

00:00:39.655 --> 00:00:42.607
solution. This is not a water-only assay.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.938
The original absorbance figure gives the numerical

00:00:48.938 --> 00:00:52.076
story. The original band at four hundred

00:00:52.076 --> 00:00:55.214
twenty-one nanometres decreases, while a strong signal

00:00:55.214 --> 00:00:58.352
emerges at five hundred twenty. The shift

00:00:58.352 --> 00:00:59.697
is ninety-nine nanometres.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.958
Most tested monovalent anions caused no comparable

00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:07.115
response. Hydroxide is the important exception: it

00:01:07.115 --> 00:01:10.273
also changed the colour. That caveat belongs

00:01:10.273 --> 00:01:12.979
beside the claim of cyanide sensing.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:19.271
Curcumin emits fluorescence around five hundred twenty

00:01:19.271 --> 00:01:22.743
nanometres. Adding cyanide quenched that emission. These

00:01:22.743 --> 00:01:26.214
are the actual fluorescence results, accompanied by

00:01:26.214 --> 00:01:27.702
photographed sample vials.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.732
Curcumin fluorescence was also observed in living

00:01:33.732 --> 00:01:36.664
cells. After cyanide was added, the signal

00:01:36.664 --> 00:01:39.596
slowly faded over time. The schematic here

00:01:39.596 --> 00:01:42.527
is illustrative; it is not a fabricated

00:01:42.527 --> 00:01:43.365
cell image.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:48.850
The reported detection limit was two point

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:51.899
three micromolar. The solvent mixture, hydroxide interference,

00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:54.949
and slow cellular response limit how broadly

00:01:54.949 --> 00:01:57.127
we can interpret this finding.
